To solve this, we first condense the nested roots by applying the exponent rules.
\begin{align*}x \sqrt{x} &= \sqrt{x} \cdot \sqrt{x} \cdot \sqrt{x}\\& = x^{3/2}\end{align*}

\begin{align*}\root 3 \of {x^{3/2}}&= \left( x^{3/2} \right)^{1/3}\\&= x^{1/2}\end{align*}

\begin{align*}\root 3 \of {x \root 3 \of {x \root 3 \of {x^{1/2}}}}&= \root 3 \of {x \root 3 \of {x \cdot x^{\frac {1}{6}}}}\\&= \root 3 \of {x \cdot x^{\frac {7}{6}}}\\&= \root 3 \of {x^{\frac {13}{6}}}\\&= x^{\frac {13}{18}}\end{align*}
That is, our final answer is $\boxed{x^{\frac {13}{18}}}$.</think> <answer>$x^{\frac {13}{18}}$</answer>

So first I tried using common tangents between ellipses. So for a general conic of the form $\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2}+\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1$, the line $y-y_1=m(x-x_1)$ is tangent if
\begin{equation}
b^2(x_1^2+y_1^2-2x_1h)-2a^2m(x_1y_1-x_1h-y_1k+k)+a^2(y_1^2-k^2)=0
\end{equation}
Then I set of $y^2=4x$ and $x^2=-32y$ to be a conic and tried to apply the equation above to find $m$.</think> <answer>$y=\frac34x+\frac{36}3$ </answer>

